\frac{2x^2-3x}{x^2-x} + 5x -11 &= \frac{2x-3}{x-1} + 5x -11. 
\end{align*}Next, simplify the right-hand side by dividing the numerator and denominator by $x^{2}-1$: \begin{align*}
\frac{3x^2+5x+2}{x^2-1} &= \frac{3x+2}{x+1}. 
\end{align*}Now, we have that \begin{align*}
\frac{2x-3}{x-1} + 5x-11 &= \frac{3x+2}{x+1}. 
\end{align*}Clearing the denominators, we get $(2x-3)(x+1)+(5x-11)(x-1)(x-1)=(3x+2)(x-1)$. Expanding and simplifying, we obtain $2x^3-8x^2-4x+8=0$. Factoring out $2$, we see that $(x-2)(2x^2-4x-4)=0$ is equivalent to providing the solutions $\boxed{2, 1+\sqrt{3}, 1-\sqrt{3}}.$</think> <answer> $2,1+\sqrt3,1-\sqrt3$</answer>

